```

With this change in place:

1. When you toggle “Parallel” / “Sequential” on your multi‐instance loop, the modeling command will call into `UpdateModdlePropertiesHandler.execute(...)`.
2. Because the `moddleElement` is a `MultiInstanceLoopCharacteristics`, your activity shape(s) get returned from `getVisualReferences`.
3. The command stack then knows to re‐render (and re‐export) those shapes, and you’ll see the XML snippet 

   ```
   <bpmn:multiInstanceLoopCharacteristics
     isSequential="true" …/>
   ```

   (or without `isSequential` when you switch back to parallel) correctly show up in your serialized XML.
